    "figures": [
        {
            "claim_index": 31,
            "claim": "1. Figure 1: Overview of Silence-Conditional Output Suppression. Given audio input, Whisper's encoder produces hidden states that are processed by the decoder. Our method extracts pno_speech from the first decoder step. If pno_speech >= τ, the output is suppressed to empty; otherwise, standard transcription proceeds. The method is training-free and requires only a single additional forward pass.",
            "verdict": "Verified",
            "explanation": "Analysis stage: The described method is exactly implemented in run_schm.py (suppress mode): p_no_speech is extracted from the first decoder step via compute_p_nospeech.py, and if p_no_speech >= tau, the output is set to empty string; otherwise standard transcription proceeds. The method uses the pre-trained model without any weight updates. Underlying behavioral data in condition_c/RESULTS.json confirms the suppression logic produces correct outputs.",
            "evidence": "exp/schm/inference/run_schm.py; exp/schm/inference/compute_p_nospeech.py; exp/EXPERIMENT_RESULTS/condition_c_schm/RESULTS.json",
            "detection_mode": "static_code_analysis",
            "decision_stage": "analysis",
            "analysis_classification": {
                "bucket": "static_verifiable"
            },
